 from HEAD is not revoked; the unsalted-hash note; the backpressure caveat; the exclusion from scanner-log commits; that public issues show `file:line`; the licence and that the binary is not in the `ard` image\n27\t- [ ] The label table says `ard:needs-human` may be set by a scanner at filing (if #215 has not already)\n28\t- [ ] CLAUDE.md Layout updated; `make lint test` passes\n29\t\n30\t**Design:** #203 · **Depends on:** #216, #221 · **Part of:** #203 · **Refs, not closes:** #203\n31\t\n32\t## Implementation plan\n33\t\n34\tChecked against `origin/main` at e488a54. Inputs: #203 (owner decisions of 2026-11-23), #215, #216, `.ard/203/triage-engineer.md`, the tech-lead and PM reviews of #203.\n35\t\n36\t### Tech lead\n37\t\n38\t**Where the line with #216 falls.** #216 lands the embed, the override line with `route: needs-human`, the `TestFSContents` and `starterTree` entries, a loader test and the `ard init` PR-body opt-out note, so the role is never embedded without its route. This PR adds end-to-end proof and docs only.\n39\t\n40\t**Dependencies.**\n41\t- Hard: #216 merged (the role files, its Dockerfile pins and its default `exclude-paths`) and #215 merged.\n42\t- Hard: #221 merged (scanner failure streaks visible on the status issue), because with GitHub secret scanning off this scanner is the only detection channel and a silent stop must not go unseen.\n43\t- None on #41, #42 or #46. No controller code changes. CLAUDE.md is in ard's own `merge.protected_paths`, so the PR gets `ard:needs-approval` once #46's merger is live.\n44\t- Merge-conflict neighbours: PR #218 (#49 error-codes) and #51 (docs scanner) edit the proposal Scanners table and CLAUDE.md line 54. The conflicts are mechanical.\n45\t\n46\t**Invariants.**\n47\t- No controller code, effects or labels change, and nothing under `.ard/` is written.\n48\t- Tests must not commit a credential-shaped literal (proposal: such fixtures \"must be built at run time\"). The integration tests generate random values at run time from split prefixes, which keeps ard's worker diff guard and a later trufflehog run on ard quiet.\n49\t- A failure message never prints a planted value. Assertions report counts, paths and fingerprints only.\n50\t\n51\t**Licence.** TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0. It is not added to the root `Dockerfile` or the published `ghcr.io/albertcbrown/ard` image (owner decision, 2026-11-23). The role's own Dockerfile (built locally) or a host install supplies the binary.\n52\t\n53\t**One PR.** About 330 changed lines, under the 1,000-line cap.\n54\t\n55\t**Who builds it.** ard's engineer worker can write it. Its `make test` does not run the parts that prove the \"Done when\", which need Docker, network and the pinned binary: `go test -tags integration ./internal/roles/`. The human approving CLAUDE.md runs those (see Verification).\n56\t\n57\t### Engineer\n58\t\n59\t**Step 0: check what #216 landed.** On `origin/main`, confirm that the starter `config.yaml` override, the `TestFSContents` and `starterTree` entries and a loader test are present, and record the role `Dockerfile`'s `ARG TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION` value. If any is missing, stop and raise it on #216; do not add it here.\n60\t\n61\t**Step 1: host integration test (new `internal/roles/trufflehog_integration_test.go`, `//go:build integration`).** Prefix helpers with `th` so they do not collide with #216's `trufflehog_test.go` in the same package.\n62\t\n63\t- `bin := os.Getenv(\"ARD_TRUFFLEHOG_BIN\")`; call `t.Skip` when it is unset, as `TestGitleaksReal` does. `needTools(t, \"jq\", \"base64\")`, and `sha256sum` or `shasum`.\n64\t- Run `$bin --version`. Fail (never skip) if it does not report the role Dockerfile's `TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION` (read from the `ARG TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION=` line of the role's `Dockerfile` by a small helper in the test), because the symlink and `Raw` behaviour under test is version-specific (Q4). The comment documents how to get the binary: the release tarball for the host OS at the pinned version, checked against the release's `trufflehog_<ver>_checksums.txt`.\n65\t- Put the binary on `PATH`: a temp `bin/` with a symlink `trufflehog -> $bin`, and `PATH=bin:` + the host `PATH`. Set `HOME` and `TMPDIR` to fresh temp dirs, like the executor's host mode.\n66\t- `thPlantRepo(t) (repo string, planted thPlanted)` builds a temp repo **at run time**. Values come from `crypto/rand` over the detector's alphabet, and prefixes are joined from pieces (`\"AK\" + \"IA\"`). Variable names stay neutral (`v1`, `v2`), so the diff guard's generic-assignment rule does not fire on the test source. The repo holds:\n67\t  - value A, an AWS-shaped key ID with its secret nearby, written to `a/one.env` and `b/two.env`;\n68\t  - value B, a credentialed URI whose `Raw` is longer than 57 bytes, so a `base64` that wraps lines in the scan would change the fingerprint and be caught, in `c/three.txt`;\n69\t  - value C on a line ending `# trufflehog:ignore`, in `d/four.txt`. It **must** be reported, because the scan passes `--no-ignore-tag`;\n70\t  - value D under `.ard/7/logs/x.log`. It must **not** be reported, because of the shipped `exclude-paths`;\n71\t  - value E written to a file in a **separate** temp dir, with a symlink `e/link.env` to it. It must **not** be reported.\n72\t\n73\t  Confirm the detectors at the pinned version while implementing. If a candidate is dropped as a known example or false positive, pick another and say why in a comment.\n74\t- Make the tree read-only (`chmod -R a-w`) as the executor does. Register a `t.Cleanup` that restores `u+w` before `TempDir` removal.\n75\t- Run `scanners/trufflehog/scan` (absolute path) with cwd = repo. Assert:\n76\t  - exit 0, and stdout decodes with `decode` (from `cve_test.go`) and with `scanner.DecodeFindings`;\n77\t  - **Oracle:** run `$bin filesystem . --json --no-update --no-verification --no-ignore-tag -x <role>/exclude-paths` in-process. Keep each result's `Raw`, or `RawV2` if `Raw` is empty, in memory only. Compute the expected set as