starter list and the Configuration line. Add only what is missing, and make sure the \"The trufflehog scanner\" paragraph covers:\n98\t- the mode: HEAD only, no history, with a history scanner as a follow-up (#224);\n99\t- the flags `--no-verification`, `--no-update`, `--no-ignore-tag`, `--fail-on-scan-errors`, and that the forbidden flags are never passed;\n100\t- the allowlist projection: only the detector, `file:line` and a fingerprint ever leave the scan (public issues show `file:line`);\n101\t- the fingerprint scheme, and that the hash is unsalted, an offline oracle for a low-entropy value that is already in the repo at HEAD, accepted;\n102\t- **gone from HEAD is not revoked**: autoclose closes as completed, and the body tells the human to rotate first;\n103\t- the backpressure caveat: at `max_open` the scanner is skipped, so new leaks go unseen until a human resolves one (scanner failure streaks are posted on the status issue, #221);\n104\t- any future \"commit scanner logs\" change must exclude this scanner;\n105\t- that on a public repo with GitHub secret scanning off this scanner is the only detection channel and cannot stop a push;\n106\t- the licence: TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0, kept out of the published `ard` image; the binary comes from the role's Dockerfile or a host install.\n107\t\n108\t`CLAUDE.md`: on line 54 (`internal/roles/`), add `scanners/trufflehog` to the starter list if #216 has not. Leave line 74 alone.\n109\t\n110\t**Error behaviour.** Only tests and docs change. The integration tests fail and never skip once `ARD_TRUFFLEHOG_BIN` is set (a version mismatch fails); the Docker test skips only when Docker is unavailable.\n111\t\n112\t**Out of scope.**\n113\t- Enabling the scanner on ard's own `.ard/`, a human PR after #222.\n114\t- Any root `Dockerfile` change or pin-parity test (AGPL-3.0, owner decision).\n115\t- History scanning (#224), verification, a `redact.trufflehog` pass, per-role `network: none`, and GitHub secret scanning.\n116\t- Any change to the role's `scan`, `findings.jq` or `Dockerfile`. Those are #216's.\n117\t\n118\t**Verification.**\n119\t- `make lint test` (worker and CI).\n120\t- The human approver, on a host with Docker, network and the pinned binary: `ARD_TRUFFLEHOG_BIN=<path> go test -tags integration -run 'Trufflehog' ./internal/roles/`. Paste the PASS lines into the PR before approving.\n121\t\n122\t**Size: M.** About 330 changed lines: host integration test about 200, Docker integration test about 90, proposal about 10, CLAUDE.md 1. Protected: `CLAUDE.md`.\n123\t\n124\t**Human follow-ups (not this PR):** after #222 lands, a PR copying `internal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/` to `.ard/scanners/trufflehog/` with the override line; the live `ard-scratch` run on #203.\n125\t\n126\t### Resolved open questions (owner, 2026-11-23)\n127\t\n128\t1. **Boundary with #216:** #216 carries the embed, the `route: needs-human` override and the starter listing tests, so the role is never embedded without its route. #217 keeps the integration and Docker tests, the docs and CLAUDE.md.\n129\t2. **`ard init` PR-body note for trufflehog:** accepted, as a fixed opt-out note; it lands in #216 with the listing tests.\n130\t3. **Licence:** TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0 and stays out of the published `ard` image. The root `Dockerfile` pin is removed from this issue's scope; the binary comes from the role's own Dockerfile (built locally) or a host install. The licence is recorded in the role's docs.\n131\t4. **`ARD_TRUFFLEHOG_BIN` at another version:** the tests fail when it is not the pinned version.\n132\t5. **Routing:** one scanner key, `route: pending | none | needs-human` (#215). trufflehog uses `needs-human`.\n133\t6. **Visibility:** #221 (scanner failure streaks on the status issue) lands before this issue.\n134\t\n135\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96f8d4a9-7666-4e99-9ffe-07f2b6088bfc","uuid":"2bd0f736-7c51-49c7-b206-67b2f65246bb","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:30:09.428Z","tool_use_result":{"type":