{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0143WXv1CTNagtheTMKJo549","type":"tool_result","content":"internal/roles:\nconfig.yaml\ncve_docker_integration_test.go\ncve_integration_test.go\ncve_test.go\ndocs_docker_integration_test.go\ndocs_test.go\neng_review_test.go\nengineer_test.go\nerrcodes_integration_test.go\nerrcodes_test.go\nlead_test.go\nlicense_review_integration_test.go\nlicense_review_test.go\nmissing_tests_test.go\nreviewers\nroles.go\nroles_test.go\nscanner_guard_test.go\nscanners\nsecurity_review_test.go\ntestdata\ntriage\ntriage_roles_test.go\ntrufflehog_test.go\nworker_engineer_test.go\nworkers\n\ninternal/roles/scanners:\ncve\ndocs\nerror-codes\nmissing-tests\ntrufflehog\n\ninternal/roles/scanners/trufflehog:\nDockerfile\nexclude-paths\nfindings.jq\nscan\ninternal/roles/trufflehog_test.go:287:\tfor _, s := range []string{\"ENV TMPDIR=/var/tmp\", \"ARG TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION=\", \"sha256sum -c\"} {\ninternal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile:25:ARG TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION=3.100.0\ninternal/roles/scanners/trufflehog/Dockerfile:38:    curl -fsSL -o /tmp/th.tgz \"https://github.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/releases/download/v${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}/trufflehog_${TRUFFLEHOG_VERSION}_linux_${TARGETARCH}.tar.gz\"; \\\ndocs/proposal.md:214:| trufflehog | leaked-credential scan of the current commit (`sh` + `jq` + TruffleHog) | 24 h | 1 | yes |\ndocs/proposal.md:225:**The trufflehog scanner** (`scanners/trufflehog`, a `sh` script plus one `jq` program) runs `trufflehog filesystem . --json --no-update --no-color --no-verification --no-ignore-tag --fail-on-scan-errors --concurrency=2` on the current commit. It never verifies a credential against a provider. Only the detector name, file, line and a hash of the secret leave the scan: `Raw`, `RawV2`, `Redacted`, `SecretParts`, `ExtraData` and `StructuredData` stay in pipes inside `scan`. The fingerprint is `trufflehog:` plus the first 16 hex digits of SHA-256 over `ard-trufflehog-v1`, a NUL byte and the base64 of the secret (an unsalted hash, so one value gives one issue wherever it appears). The scan fails closed: a non-zero trufflehog exit, a missing `finished scanning` summary, zero chunks on a non-empty tree, or a result count that differs from the summary produces no findings, so nothing is autoclosed on a partial run. `exclude-paths` (regexes; `.git` is always excluded) and `allow` (one fingerprint per line) are human-owned; a bad `allow` entry fails the run. Findings use `route: needs-human`, severity high, and carry a runbook that says to rotate the credential first. `commit` is the scanned SHA, recorded in `.ard/<n>/issue.md`; history is not scanned. TruffleHog is AGPL-3.0: it is installed by the role's Dockerfile and is not in the published `ard` image.\ndocs/proposal.md:428:  scanners/trufflehog:      { every: 24h, max_open: 5, group_size: 1, autoclose: true, route: needs-human, timeout: 30m }\ndocs/proposal.md:442:**`ard init` proposes the starter `.ard/` as a PR (decided, #27).** It builds `config.yaml` and the starter roles in memory (today `scanners/cve`, `scanners/docs`, `scanners/error-codes`, `scanners/trufflehog`, `triage/lead`, `triage/engineer`, `workers/engineer`, `reviewers/eng-review`, `reviewers/license-review` and `reviewers/security-review`; `intake: {mode: label}`, the protected-path defaults above, and the cve, docs, error-codes, lead, engineer, worker, eng-review, security-review and license-review overrides), compares them with `main`, commits them on a new branch `ard-init` cut from `main` through the effect layer and a narrow committer lane, pushes it and opens a PR. It writes nothing to the local working tree or to `main`, and `scan` is committed `100755`. Files that already exist on `main` with different contents are a conflict naming the paths; `--force` proposes overwriting them, and init never deletes anything. It refuses while `ard-init` exists on the remote, whatever its PR's state, so it never force-pushes over or stacks commits on a human's edits: merge or close the PR, delete the branch and rerun. If `main` already has every starter file it prints `nothing to propose`. It syncs the label catalogue first (like `ard labels sync`), so a failure leaves nothing pushed. With `--dry-run` the commit, push and PR are logged to the ledger instead of acting. A missing repo, credentials or `main` branch exits 1 with nothing written, and `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN` auth is refused outside `--dry-run`. The PR body carries the one step the App cannot do: copy `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` and set the repository variable `ARD_BOT_LOGIN` (optionally `ARD_BOT_CHECK_SINCE`). It also says to merge with **Squash and merge** or **Create a merge commit**, never a fast-forward from the command line, which would put the bot's commit on main's first-parent history. **Rebase and merge** is also safe: the scratch-repo run (#85) showed GitHub records the merging human as committer of a rebase-merged commit (the bot stays the author), and the bot-commit check keys on committer, so it does not flag it. The body still names only the two merges above.\ninternal/roles/cve_docker_integration_test.go:23:func dockerOut(t *testing.T, timeout time.Duration, args ...string) (stdout, stderr string, code int) {\ninternal/roles/cve_docker_integration_test.go:42:func scanRunArgs(image, repo, roleDir string, extraEnv ...string) []string {\ninternal/roles/cve_test.go:15:func needTools(t *testing.T, names ...string) {\ninternal/roles/cve_test.go:139:func decode(t *testing.T, b []byte) []finding {\ninternal/roles/trufflehog_test.go","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96f8d4a9-7666-4e99-9ffe-07f2b6088bfc","uuid":"8ff150d8-65af-491c-ac01-d89be867023c","timestamp":"2026-11-23T22:30:12.868Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"internal/roles:\nconfig.yaml\ncve_docker_integration_test.go\ncve_integration_test.go\ncve_test.go\ndocs_docker_integration_test.go\ndocs_test.go\neng_review_test.go\nengineer_test.g