lse fail) stdout equals a host-mode run byte for byte, otherwise structure only (3 findings, A's two files, fingerprints match `^trufflehog:[0-9a-f]{16}$`). The symlink dangles in the container, so only the host test proves symlinks are not followed.\n3. `docs/proposal.md`, \"The trufflehog scanner\" paragraph (line ~225): add only what is missing: HEAD only with a history scanner as a follow-up (#224); the flags and that forbidden flags are never passed; public issues show `file:line`; the unsalted hash as an accepted offline oracle for a low-entropy value already at HEAD; gone from HEAD is not revoked (autoclose closes as completed, the body says to rotate first); backpressure caveat (at `max_open` the scanner is skipped, new leaks go unseen until a human resolves one; failure streaks appear on the status issue, #221); any future commit-scanner-logs change must exclude this scanner; with GitHub secret scanning off on a public repo this scanner is the only detection channel and cannot stop a push; the licence (AGPL-3.0, binary from the role's Dockerfile or a host install). The label table already says a scanner may set `ard:needs-human` at filing (line ~81), so leave it. Do not touch the root `Dockerfile`.\n4. `CLAUDE.md`: no edit (see note above). `docs/layout.md` already lists the role; add the two test files only if the file lists test files (it does not appear to).\n\n### Test plan\n- `TestTrufflehogReal` and `TestTrufflehogDocker` as above, in the two new files. Run by hand: `ARD_TRUFFLEHOG_BIN=<path> go test -tags integration -run Trufflehog ./internal/roles/` (Docker, network and the pinned binary needed). They are not run by `make test`.\n- Failure cases: `ARD_TRUFFLEHOG_BIN` at another version must fail, not skip; unset skips the host test only.\n- Edge cases: `Raw` over 57 bytes (base64 line wrapping), ignore tag, excluded path, dangling or followed symlink, read-only tree.\n- Gate: `make lint test` (compiles nothing with the integration tag, so also run `go vet -tags integration ./internal/roles/`).\n\n### Risk\nLow. Tests and docs only, no controller code, no `.ard/` writes. No protected path from `merge.protected_paths` is touched if CLAUDE.md stays unchanged (it would need human approval if edited). The worker cannot run the integration tests, so a human must run them and paste the results into the PR. Main hazard: a planted value leaking into a failure message or a committed literal; the plan forbids both.\n\n### Size\nM (about 300 changed lines). Files: `internal/roles/trufflehog_integration_test.go` (new), `internal/roles/trufflehog_docker_integration_test.go` (new), `docs/proposal.md`.\nEOF\ncat > .ard/217/triage-engineer.md <<'EOF'\n---\nrole: engineer\nstatus: done\nattempt: 1\n---\nAdds host and Docker integration tests for the trufflehog scanner role, both failing when the binary is not the pinned version, and fills the gaps in the proposal's trufflehog paragraph. Size M, risk low, since only tests and docs change.\n\n## Open issues\n- CLAUDE.md no longer has the Layout line the issue describes: Layout now points to docs/layout.md, which already lists the trufflehog role. The plan therefore leaves CLAUDE.md unchanged, so the checklist item for it is already met and no protected-path approval is needed.\n- The integration tests need Docker, the network and the pinned binary. A maintainer must run them by hand and record the results on the pull request, because `make test` does not run them.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":626,"cache_read_input_tokens":30419,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":626},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"96f8d4a9-7666-4e99-9ffe-07f2b6088bfc